{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Moderate upstream boost to replenish node2 backlog while slightly reducing node0 order to avoid overloading node1, and keeping node1 order near HAPPO to maintain flow.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0",
          "delta": "-1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1",
          "delta": "0"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2",
          "delta": "2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Pipeline-aware relaxation: reduce orders when pipeline is high relative to recent demand, and increase when backlog is high and pipeline low. Node0 reduces due to high backlog and pipeline, node1 reduces due to high pipeline, node2 increases due to high backlog and low inventory.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and pipeline>40",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and pipeline>30",
          "delta": "-1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>20 and pipeline<70",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and pipeline>=70",
          "delta": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Coordinated response to demand surge: increase all orders slightly to build inventory, but cap node0 increase to avoid excessive upstream backlog, and boost node2 more to clear its backlog.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and growth>1.2",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and growth>1.2",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and growth>1.2",
          "delta": "3"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Pipeline-aware relaxation: when recent demand is below baseline, reduce orders to avoid excess inventory, but only if pipeline is low to prevent starvation. Node0 has pipeline 13, so reduce by 2. Node1 and Node2 have no pipeline, so keep orders unchanged to avoid starving downstream.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and growth < 1 and pipeline < 10",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and growth < 1 and pipeline >= 10",
          "delta": "-1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 1 and backlog > 0",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 2 and backlog > 0",
          "delta": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Coordinated correction: increase orders when backlog exists to clear it, and reduce orders when inventory is high and recent demand is low. Node0 has high inventory and low growth, so reduce. Node1 and Node2 have high inventory but no backlog, so reduce slightly to avoid excess.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "backlog > 0",
          "delta": "min(2, backlog)"
        },
        {
          "when": "inventory > 20 and growth < 1",
          "delta": "-1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and inventory > 10 and growth < 1",
          "delta": "-1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Emergency response: increase orders when recent demand exceeds baseline (growth > 1) to build pipeline, but only if pipeline is low. Also increase orders if backlog is high. Otherwise, keep orders near HAPPO to avoid overreaction.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "growth > 1 and pipeline < 5",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "backlog > 2",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and pipeline < 3 and growth > 0.9",
          "delta": "1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Node0: if backlog positive, increase order by 2 to clear backlog faster; else if inventory low and pipeline low, increase by 1. Node1: if backlog positive, increase by 2; else if inventory low and pipeline low, increase by 1. Node2: if backlog positive, increase by 2; else if inventory low and pipeline low, increase by 1. This aims to reduce backlog and prevent stockouts.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and inventory<5 and pipeline<20",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and inventory<10 and pipeline<20",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and inventory<10 and pipeline<20",
          "delta": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Node0: if backlog positive, increase by 3; else if inventory low and pipeline low, increase by 2. Node1: if backlog positive, increase by 3; else if inventory low and pipeline low, increase by 2. Node2: if backlog positive, increase by 3; else if inventory low and pipeline low, increase by 2. Stronger response to backlog and low inventory.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and inventory<5 and pipeline<20",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and inventory<10 and pipeline<20",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "3"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and inventory<10 and pipeline<20",
          "delta": "2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Node0: if backlog positive, increase by 2; else if inventory low and pipeline low, increase by 1. Node1: if backlog positive, increase by 2; else if inventory low and pipeline low, increase by 1. Node2: if backlog positive, increase by 2; else if inventory low and pipeline low, increase by 1. Additionally, if growth>1.1, increase all nodes by 1 to preempt demand surge.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and inventory<5 and pipeline<20",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and inventory<10 and pipeline<20",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and inventory<10 and pipeline<20",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "growth>1.1",
          "delta": "1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Refine best prior candidate (llm_r1_0) by keeping node0 reduction and node1 neutral, but making node2 boost more responsive to backlog and pipeline: if node2 backlog is high and pipeline is not excessive, boost more; if pipeline is very high, reduce boost to avoid upstream backlog.",
      "rules": [
        {"when": "agent==0", "delta": "-1"},
        {"when": "agent==1", "delta": "0"},
        {"when": "agent==2 and backlog>20 and pipeline<70", "delta": "3"},
        {"when": "agent==2 and pipeline>=70", "delta": "1"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Refinement of zero-correction baseline. The emergency is not yet visible in recent demand (growth 0.83), but downstream node0 has pipeline 13 and no backlog, while upstream nodes have zero pipeline. To avoid starving downstream after delay, add small pipeline-aware replenishment at nodes 1 and 2 only when their pipeline is empty and they have no backlog, so they can support future node0 orders. Node0 stays near HAPPO to avoid excess inventory given low recent demand. All deltas are small and coordinated.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent == 1 and pipeline == 0 and backlog == 0 and inventory < 40",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 2 and pipeline == 0 and backlog == 0 and inventory < 40",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 0",
          "delta": "min(2, backlog)"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and growth < 1 and pipeline >= 10",
          "delta": "-1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
